<title>UK: Ashquay says to borrow for UK Estate shares.</title>
<headline>Ashquay says to borrow for UK Estate shares.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Ashquay Group Plc said on Monday that it would borrow up to 750,000 stg on normal commercial terms to acquire shares in property development firm UK Estates Plc.</p>
<p>Ashquay, which is making a hostile bid for UK Estates, said it would borrow the money from Close Brothers Ltd, a subsidiary of Close Brothers Finance Ltd, financial adviser to Ashquay.  </p>
<p>Monday is the closing date for Ashquay's bid  in which Ashquay has offered 10 shares for every 13 ordinary shares in the property development firm.</p>
<p>Ashquay has earlier said it owned or had acceptances for 38 percent of UK Estates's ordinary share capital.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +0171-542 7717</p>
